+# Live research record
+
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1**
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Used for: confirming the documented VCF 5.2.x-to-9.1 upgrade path, mandatory management services, and ordered component sequence.
+
+- **Could not retrieve binary for component during Deploy and Validate in VCF 9.1**
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/436258/could-not-retrieve-binary-for-component.html
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Used for: checking the active VCF 9.1 BOM component builds for SDDC Manager, NSX, and vCenter.
+
+- **Upgrade failure due to the VCF back-in-time restriction**
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135/upgrade-failure-for-vcenter-80-u3j-esxi.html
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Used for: cross-checking the ESX, vCenter, and NSX target component builds and the interoperability gate that blocks chronologically older targets.
+
+- **Broadcom Compatibility Guide**
+  URL: https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Used for: checking that the target host/storage design must be evaluated as an ESA-capable hardware profile rather than treating an OSA cluster as an in-place ESA conversion.
+
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix**
+  URL: https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Used for: cross-checking the component combination and target-version interoperability represented in the target BOM.
+
+- **How to convert a vSAN OSA cluster to a vSAN ESA cluster**
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/432894/how-to-convert-a-vsan-osa-original-stora.html
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Used for: confirming that OSA-to-ESA is not an in-place conversion and requires a new or redeployed ESA cluster plus workload migration.
